      "id": 1792775975487,
      "created_at": "2026-10-23T17:19:35.487Z",
      "title": "\\oint_C \\left( (e^x - y^3) \\, dx + ",
      "type": "expression",
      "query": "\\oint_C \\left( (e^x - y^3) \\, dx + (x^3 + \\sin y) \\, dy \\right)",
      "answer": "24\\pi",
      "steps": [
        {
          "label": "Given line integral along closed boundary C:",
          "katex": "\\oint_C (e^x - y^3)\\,dx + (x^3 + \\sin y)\\,dy"
        },
        {
          "label": "Step 1: Identify vector field components M and N:",
          "katex": "M = e^x - y^3 \\implies \\frac{\\partial M}{\\partial y} = -3y^2, \\quad N = x^3 + \\sin y \\implies \\frac{\\partial N}{\\partial x} = 3x^2"
        },
        {
          "label": "Step 2: Apply Green's Theorem ∬_D (∂N/∂x - ∂M/∂y) dA:",
          "katex": "\\frac{\\partial N}{\\partial x} - \\frac{\\partial M}{\\partial y} = 3x^2 - (-3y^2) = 3(x^2 + y^2)"
        },
        {
          "label": "Step 3: Convert region D enclosed by circular boundary (radius R = 2) to polar coordinates:",
          "katex": "I = \\int_0^{2\\pi} \\int_0^2 3(r^2) \\cdot r \\, dr \\, d\\theta = 3 \\int_0^{2\\pi} d\\theta \\int_0^2 r^3 \\, dr"
        },
        {
          "label": "Step 4: Evaluate definite polar integrals:",
          "katex": "I = 3(2\\pi) \\left[ \\frac{r^4}{4} \\right]_0^2 = 6\\pi \\left(\\frac{16}{4}\\right) = 24\\pi"
        },
        {
          "label": "Final Circulation Value:",
          "katex": "\\mathbf{\\oint_C M\\,dx + N\\,dy = 24\\pi}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 1792775964776,
      "created_at": "2026-10-23T17:19:24.776Z",
      "title": "\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{(-1)^n (x",
      "type": "expression",
      "query": "\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{(-1)^n (x - 2)^n}{n \\cdot 4^n} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\sum_{n=2}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{n (\\ln n)^p}",
      "answer": "\\text{Series 1: } x \\in (-2, 6], \\; R = 4; \\quad \\text{Series 2: Converges for } p > 1, \\; \\text{Diverges for } p \\le 1",
      "steps": [
        {
          "label": "Given dual infinite series convergence problem:",
          "katex": "\\text{Series 1: } \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\frac{(-1)^n (x - 2)^n}{n \\cdot 4^n}, \\qquad \\text{Series 2: } \\sum_{n=2}^\\infty \\frac{1}{n (\\ln n)^p}"
        },
        {
          "label": "Step 1: Ratio Test on Series 1 to find Radius of Convergence R:",
          "katex": "L = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\left| \\frac{a_{n+1}}{a_n} \\right| = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\left| \\frac{(x - 2)^{n+1}}{(n+1)4^{n+1}} \\cdot \\frac{n 4^n}{(x - 2)^n} \\right| = \\frac{|x - 2|}{4} \\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\frac{n}{n + 1} = \\frac{|x - 2|}{4}"
        },
        {
          "label": "Step 2: Condition for absolute convergence (L < 1):",
          "katex": "\\frac{|x - 2|}{4} < 1 \\implies |x - 2| < 4 \\implies R = 4, \\quad -2 < x < 6"
        },
        {
          "label": "Step 3: Test endpoints of interval of convergence:",
          "katex": "\\text{At } x = -2: \\; \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\frac{(-1)^n (-4)^n}{n 4^n} = \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\frac{1}{n} \\; (\\text{Harmonic series } \\implies \\text{Diverges}) \\\\[4pt] \\text{At } x = 6: \\; \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\frac{(-1)^n 4^n}{n 4^n} = \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\frac{(-1)^n}{n} \\; (\\text{Alternating harmonic series } \\implies \\text{Converges})"
        },
        {
          "label": "Step 4: Conclusion for Series 1 Interval of Convergence:",
          "katex": "\\mathbf{I = (-2, 6], \\quad R = 4}"
        },
        {
          "label": "Step 5: Apply Cauchy Integral Test on Series 2 (f(x) = 1 / [x (ln x)^p]):",
          "katex": "\\int_2^\\infty \\frac{1}{x (\\ln x)^p} \\, dx = \\int_{\\ln 2}^\\infty u^{-p} \\, du \\quad (\\text{where } u = \\ln x, \\; du = \\frac{dx}{x})"
        },
        {
          "label": "Step 6: Conclusion for Series 2 Convergence:",
          "katex": "\\mathbf{\\text{Converges if and only if } p > 1; \\quad \\text{Diverges for } p \\le 1}"
        }
      ]
    }
